    engine2d_strict_vulkan_evidence_fails_after_shared_session_example_2026-08-19, 1, "2026-11-13: On release/1.0.0 c8c3e7bc4f1, Linux aarch64 (DGX Spark GB10), Rust seed af717f53d6bce3e5: test/02_integration/rendering/engine2d_embedded_surface_spec.spl 10 examples, 8 passed, 2 failed. The two Vulkan-evidence examples this record names pass (uses the Vulkan device path only for preflighted root and named-child compositions; composites preflighted resolved text through checked Vulkan image blending); whether their Ok(engine) arm or their Err arm ran was not instrumented, so this is not device evidence. Red: (1) the WM example, on fixture oracles that no longer match the product (expected 40 to equal 51: commands[0] is now the 0x28 shadow rect; content rect is 14,68 112x44 against a 120x52 fixture frame, so the fail-closed placeholder is drawn); (2) opacity_milli=500, 126 vs 127. Not changed here: correcting (1) rewrites six oracles and needs the spec owner to confirm the 4px content inset is intended."

